Provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sherd is a clean-room implementation. It is written from a functional
specification derived from publicly documented behavior, published file-format
documentation, and externally observable application behavior. It contains no
decompiled code, no copied source, and no copied assets from any proprietary
product. See section 0 of REQUIREMENT_SPEC.md.

"Sherd" is a working codename. It is not a claim to any trademark, and it
must clear a trademark search before any public release (LEG-003, OD-007).
